=== empty lists are syntax errors
[if then fi] status 2
[if true; then fi] status 2
[if true; then :; elif then :; fi] status 2
[if true; then :; else fi] status 2
[while do done] status 2
[until false; do done] status 2
[for x in a; do done] status 2
[{ }] status 2
[( )] status 2
[f() { }] status 2
=== non-empty lists and empty case items still work
[if true; then :; fi] status 0
[while false; do :; done] status 0
[case x in x) ;; esac] status 0
[{ :; }] status 0
